            ("How big is the refraction?", "At the horizon, the average refraction is 34 arcminutes (0.57°) for a standard atmosphere, and it falls off rapidly with height: only 1 arcminute at 45°. The refraction depends on the temperature and the pressure, which is why the values are 10–20% larger on cold days. Because of it, the Sun appears to rise about 3 minutes earlier and set about 3 minutes later at mid-latitudes than the geometry alone would give."),
